    <unit id="extconf.additionalReadOnlyTables">
      <segment>
        <source>Additional read-only tables: comma-separated list of tables without workspace support that MCP may read (e.g. sys_file). The workspace-aware write tools never write them.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.additionalStandaloneTables">
      <segment>
        <source>Additional standalone tables: comma-separated list of tables that are hidden in the backend (e.g. sys_file_metadata) but may be read and written through MCP as standalone records.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.sessionTimeout">
      <segment>
        <source>Session timeout (seconds): idle lifetime of session-based MCP clients. Expired sessions answer with HTTP 404 and need a new handshake; stateless clients are unaffected. Default: 14400 (4 hours).</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.fileSandboxRoot">
      <segment>
        <source>File sandbox root: combined identifier of the folder the MCP file tools work in, e.g. 1:/mcp/ (fileadmin/mcp/ in the default storage).</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.workspaceUploadSubfolders">
      <segment>
        <source>Workspace upload folders: store MCP uploads in a subfolder per workspace below the sandbox root, so drafts stay apart.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.maxFileSizeMb">
      <segment>
        <source>Maximum file size (MiB): upper limit for base64 payloads, files fetched from URLs and pre-signed uploads of the UploadFile and UploadFileFromUrl tools. Default: 500.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.allowedOrigins">
      <segment>
        <source>Allowed browser origins: comma-separated list of exact http(s) origins that browser-based MCP clients may call from. The site itself is always allowed.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.enableMcpAuthHeaderDiagnostic">
      <segment>
        <source>Authorization header check: enable the public ?test=auth diagnostic on the MCP endpoint, which the backend connection check uses. Keep it off on hardened sites that do not need it.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.localUnsafeMode">
      <segment>
        <source>Local development mode: relax workspace-only writes, the non-workspace table block and the file sandbox, so MCP can edit live records and write anywhere in fileadmin. "auto" detects DDEV and the TYPO3 Development context. User TSconfig options.mcpServer.localUnsafeMode overrides this; options.mcpServer.strictSandbox or the feature flag mcpServer.strictSandbox forces strict mode. Never enable it in production.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.enforceCapabilityManifest">
      <segment>
        <source>Enforce the capability manifest: reject every tool call whose required subsystems are not declared in Configuration/Capabilities.yaml. Turn it off for debugging only.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.schemaDetail">
      <segment>
        <source>Tool schema detail: verbosity of tools/list. "Concise" (default) condenses long tool and field descriptions so a client spends far fewer context-window tokens per session; the full text of any tool stays available through the GetCapabilities tool. "Full" sends every description verbatim.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.localUnsafeMode.auto">
      <segment>
        <source>Auto-detect (DDEV / Development context)</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.localUnsafeMode.on">
      <segment>
        <source>Always on (UNSAFE — local development only)</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.localUnsafeMode.off">
      <segment>
        <source>Always off (production default)</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.schemaDetail.concise">
      <segment>
        <source>Concise (lean tools/list, saves context-window tokens)</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="extconf.schemaDetail.full">
      <segment>
        <source>Full (verbose descriptions)</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
